{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The digital caliper feels useful now because it would help me check screw diameters and match parts from my recent hardware assortments.",
    "The grommet assortment and fastening tape partly fit my interest in small hardware and mounting supplies, although I would wait for a specific need before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The safety can, marine adhesive, cutting wheels and feeler gauge serve tasks I have not shown a need for; buying hooks and fasteners does not mean I am doing those jobs.",
    "The SAE nut assortment is not a clear match for my recent metric screws, while eighteen rolls of tape and a thousand gloves are excessive for my occasional needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in small hardware seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop supply.",
    "Assortments and multipacks seem to be treated as appealing regardless of whether the parts fit my existing hardware or the quantity is useful to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: my recent M3, M4 and M5 screws make matching metric hardware more relevant than an SAE assortment.",
    "I interact infrequently and need a concrete use before choosing something; a tool for matching my existing parts has a clearer purpose than supplies for an unrelated repair."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in hardware and mounting supplies but often miss the specific fit and immediate usefulness that would make me choose an item."
}"}
